<newsitem itemid="164949" id="root" date="1996-11-04" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Greycoat H1 pretax profit rises sharply.</title>
<headline>Greycoat H1 pretax profit rises sharply.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.1		    vs 1.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 none		   vs none</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    3.8		    vs 1.7</p>
<p>NOTE - UK property company Greycoat Plc said it had not declared an interim dividend but &quot;expects to recommend a dividend for the year to March 31 1997 of 1.2 pence net per ordinary share, a 50 percent increase over the 0.8 pence net (for the previous year)&quot;.  </p>
<p> Gross rental income    17.3		   vs 18.4</p>
<p> Property management    0.3		    vs 0.3</p>
<p> Turnover		   17.6		   vs 18.7</p>
<p> Operating profit	 15.1		   vs 15.8</p>
<p> Profit from disposals  0.6		    vs nil</p>
<p> Finance costs	    11.4		   vs 14.1</p>
<p> Tax credit		 0.2		    vs none</p>
<p> Attributable	     4.0		    vs 1.7</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
